    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipe summary\n| category = Eggplant recipes\n| servings = 2 persons\n| time = 15 minutes\n| difficulty = 2\n| image = [[File:Grilled Aubergine and Pesto Sandwich03.jpg|300px]]\n| energy = \n| note = \n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Japan|Japanese Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian]]\n== Ingredients ==\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. (375 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) large [[Cookbook:Eggplant|aubergine]] (eggplant)\n* [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|Vegetable oil]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Miso|miso]] paste\n* 1½ tablespoons [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 2 tablespoons soup [[Cookbook:Stock|stock]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] white [[Cookbook:Sesame Seed|sesame seeds]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Wash the aubergine, and cut it into 2.5 cm [[Cookbook:Slicing|slices]] lengthwise.  \n# [[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] the cut surfaces with oil.  \n# [[Cookbook:Grilling|Grill]] 7–10 cm from the source of the heat until the aubergine is tender and browned all over (about 5 minutes).\n# In a small saucepan combine the miso, sugar, and soup stock. Cook, stirring, over low heat until the mixture is smooth and hot. Do not let it [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]].  \n# Pour the sauce mixture over the aubergine.  \n# In a small frying pan toast the sesame seeds until they jump, then sprinkle them over the aubergine.\n\n[[Category:Japanese recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using eggplant]]\n[[Category:Grilled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using miso]]",
